ok - the board stays off unless a regular, valid, enabled config opts in
ok - an empty fleet renders its empty state with idle registered projects folded away
ok - a board whose payload exceeds one environment string still builds and renders
ok - doing now holds the tasks with a worker, next what starts automatically, charted next what waits, and every task sits in exactly one lane
ok - each project's Doing now lists its workers one line each with a plain status, and the page has no separate Workers section
ok - a worker's line is worded from the resolved current state, and one waiting on the captain or finished stays in charted next
ok - a second mate's workers and queued work sit in their project's lanes, and a home that could not be read is named
ok - repository fallback leads with real questions and explained options, then the three lanes
ok - each card leads with project, what it is about and what it is for; an unexplained one says so and still answers
ok - a project map groups work under the captain's names; unmatched work and bad maps fall back by repository
ok - the table of contents lists every card and quiet project in page order, and each entry jumps to its own
ok - every card collapses and expands from a real button, stays that way across reloads, and a contents jump expands it
ok - each project shows a timeline of its pull requests, and a merge with a failed run is marked by shape and word
ok - pointing at or focusing a pull request shows what changed in plain words and whether the runs after its merge succeeded
ok - pressing a pull request pins its detail with a link to it, across reloads, until it is pressed again or closed
ok - a project whose merges start no run says so, and a project whose pull requests could not be read is named
ok - a pull request belongs to the named project its task belongs to
ok - the pull request read is cached outside the directory Lavish serves
ok - pull requests are read at most once per interval, and a failed or hung read keeps the last good timeline and says so
ok - a merge waiting for its runs is drawn as running, and one whose only run was cancelled as replaced
ok - the newest merge stays on the strip however long ago its pull request was opened
ok - a project that could not be read says why, and only a read that found nothing says no pull requests were found
ok - each card shows its environments: the last change in each, its runs, what still waits before it, and unknown with the reason
ok - environments follow the captain's project names, and a project with no repository says nothing
ok - an invalid environment list is named in the board notes, and a home without one says nothing about environments
